      "sequence_position": 68,
      "problem": "Let $I=[0,2]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}={i}\\times [0,i].$ Which of the following represents ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the union of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *at least one* set:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one}\\,\\,k\\in I}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=1,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}={1}\\times [0,1]={(1,k)\\,:\\,k\\in [0,1]}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a vertical line segment from the point $(1,0)$ to the point $(1,1)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14110945/assets/71dd97607df48caf579c2e476520507ede035f65c336064f022cd900b6c120fc.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}={i}\\times [0,i]={(i,k)\\,:\\,k\\in [0,i]}\n$$\n\nis the vertical line segment from the point $(i,0)$ to the point $(i,i).$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14110945/assets/4b87c830620f54e5b3a3bb7923be971b4d9d4abb98cfb3dcdc8387f376a0b452.png)\n\nAs $i$ runs over $I,$ these line segments sweep the following triangle that represents the union ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14110945/assets/6b5b39546eabacdf948bd87e793727fdc8cd8f2664df037be53bfb630fc41670.png)",
